  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="76.1b">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IICn">II Cn</ref> 76.1b</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="76.1b" corresp="#wit-g-a">⁊ ne mæg nan wif hyre bondan forbeodan, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> he ne mote into his coton gelogian þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> he wylle.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="76.1b" corresp="#wit-a">And ne mæg nan wif hyre bondan forbeodan, þæt he ne mote into his cotan gelaðyan þæt þæt he wille.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="76.1b" corresp="#wit-q">Non potest uxor aliqua sponsum suum prohibere, quin mittat in tugurio suo quod uelit (uult).</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="76.1b" corresp="#wit-b">And ne mæg nan wif hire bundan forbeodan þæt he ne mote into his cotan gelegian þæt þæt he wille.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a">And ne mæg nan wif hyre bondan forbeodan, þæt he ne mote into his coton gelogian þæt þæt he wylle.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b">But no wife can forbid her husband to deposit anything that he desires in his cottage.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a">Yet no wife can prevent her husband from storing anything he wishes in his home.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock">And no wife can forbid her husband to place inside his cottage what he pleases.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">Jedoch darf keine Frau ihrem Mann verbieten, dass er was er wolle in seine Hütte absetzen (legen B; einführen oder abladen ? A) dürfe.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">But no wife may forbid her husband to put down (lay, B; bring in or unload?, A) in his cottage whatever he wants.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="364"><ref target="clause:Ine_57">Ine 57</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">Vgl. Ine 57?</note>
        <note type="editorial">Liebermann suggests A's ‘gelaðyan’ stands for ‘gelædan’ or ‘gehladan’. He compares (with a query) Ine 57.</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">gelogian: gelaðyan A</note>
      </div>
    </body>
